      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"direction: ltr; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transfo=
rm: none; margin: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">Hi</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">=C2=A0</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">I
          received an offline comment from a senior IETF participant
          suggesting that I had misunderstood the draft and that the key
          reuse in question referred to reuse within a single session.
          That is not accurate. The draft talks about static keys, i.e.,
          keys used in more than one key-establishment.</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">=C2=A0</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">Given
          the apparent confusion between 1. reuse of ephemeral keys
          within a session, 2. reuse of ephemeral keys across sessions,
          and 3. static keys, each of which carries distinct privacy and
          security implications, I recommend that the AD ensure that all
          not yet published drafts use very precise terminology.
          Specifically, a key used in more than one key-establishment
          should use the well-established term =E2=80=9Cstatic key=E2=80=9D=
=2E</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">=C2=A0</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">---</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">=C2=A0</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">1.
          Reuse of ephemeral keys within a session:</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">=C2=A0</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">-
          Session A: ClientHello with MLKEM768 KeyShareEntry1 and
          X25519MLKEM768 KeyShareEntry2 both containing the same ML-KEM
          public key.</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">=C2=A0</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">2.
          Reuse of ephemeral keys across sessions:</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">=C2=A0</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">-
          Session B1. ClientHello with MLKEM768 KeyShareEntry3 and
          X25519 KeyShareEntry4. Sever picks X25519 KeyShareEntry4.</span=
></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">=C2=A0</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">-
          Session B2. ClientHello with MLKEM768 KeyShareEntry3 and
          X25519 KeyShareEntry5.</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; margin=
: 0cm;">
        <span
style=3D"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0=
, 0);">=C2=A0</span></p>
      <p class=3D"MsoNormal"
